## Three strongest results

1. **Hard constraints (DR1).** The brief's additive formula puts {{derived.dr1_hard_constraints.brief_additive_violations}}
   hard-constraint violations in the top-10s of {{derived.dr1_hard_constraints.n_trips}} holdout trips
   ({{derived.dr1_hard_constraints.brief_additive_trips_with_violation}} trips affected); the shipped multiplicative, hard-gated
   utility has {{derived.dr1_hard_constraints.shipped_multiplicative_gated_violations}}.
2. **Exposure bias is measured, not assumed.** The NDCG@10 gap between the biased log and the
   random-exposure holdout is {{bias_gap.popularity.gap|+.3f}} for popularity but only
   {{bias_gap.lambdamart_ips.gap|+.3f}} for the IPS-trained primary; the headline is computed on the unbiased holdout.
3. **Oracle-free selection.** Every choice (retriever K by a pre-registered rule, features, LR
   regularisation, ranker sweep) was made on train-carved validation; the true-utility oracle scored
   results but never chose anything (firewall tests + `poi_rank.cli audit --deep`).

## What was missed, and why (full scorecard: `docs/RESULTS.md`)

- **Late-found bug, fixed** (`docs/TECHNICAL.md` section 5.1): train-time traveler features contained each
  trip's own labelled browsing session. As first tagged the ranker looked no better than cosine
  ({{h_experiments.pre_fix_headline.ndcg10_primary|.4f}} vs {{h_experiments.pre_fix_headline.ndcg10_content_cosine|.4f}}); after the fix it is well above
  it. The fix also moved scorecard rows the other way: confidence-decile Spearman
  {{h_experiments.pre_fix_headline.confidence_decile_spearman|.3f}} → {{confidence_decile_validation.spearman_rho|.3f}} and scenario-4 flip overlap
  {{h_experiments.pre_fix_headline.scenario4_overlap|.3f}} → {{scenarios.overlap_matrix.diagnostic_vs_base_jaccard|.3f}}; both now MISSED.
- % of oracle ceiling {{systems.lambdamart_ips.pct_of_ceiling_ndcg10|.1%}} (target 70%); within/cross-archetype ratio
  {{personalization.archetype.within_cross_ratio|.2f}} (target 2.0); localness index rho {{localness_validation.spearman_rho|.3f}} (target 0.6).
- Long-tail share {{longtail.share|.3f}} (target 0.25); precision {{longtail.precision|.3f}} is a
  {{derived.longtail_lift_over_base_rate.final_after_mmr|.3f}}x lift over the pool base rate — the 0.40 target was set without reference to that rate.
- `make reproduce` {{~reproduce_vs_target}}; DR5 (ANN benchmark) not run. All data is synthetic.
